<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  The same group as the iOS file beside this one, spelled the way macOS demands: an app group
	  identifier has to begin with the team identifier there, and with "group." on iOS, and neither
	  platform accepts the other's spelling. One target builds for both, so the entitlements file is
	  chosen per SDK -- see CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=macosx*].

	  TS_APP_GROUP comes from Xcode-config/Shared.xcconfig, because a group has to be registered to
	  the team that signs it and a fork under another team needs its own. On this platform that is
	  the only place the identifier is written: ROMStore reads it back out of the running process's
	  entitlements with SecTask rather than keeping a copy that could disagree with this one. iOS
	  has no SecTask, so there the same value is also carried in the Info.plist -- from the same
	  build setting, so the two cannot drift.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(TeamIdentifierPrefix)$(TS_APP_GROUP)</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
